      "writtenOn": "2025-02-25T23:16:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The plan is to move to memfd in android 17.",
      "parentUuid": "672009dd_0c39603c",
      "revId": "07f3b22131a4f19ef88eaa3b25afcc0ee4292cad",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fe4c21b2_ed7b4c92",
        "filename": "libcutils/ashmem-dev.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 510,
      "author": {
        "id": 1934715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-25T23:16:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is fine for ashmem, but not for memfd files. memfd files have different naming conventions. Consider a memfd created with `memfd_create(\"test-buf\", ...)`.\n\nUsing `readlink()` on the path that points to the memfd in `/proc/self/fd/` will yield the following string: `/memfd:test-buf (deleted)`, so you have to allocate the worst case buffer size:\n\n1 (for the / character) + 6 (for the memfd: prefix) + 249 (for the max string length of the name argument in `memfd_create()` [2]) + 10 (for the \" (deleted)\" string) + 1 for the NUL terminator, which adds up to 267 bytes.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 510,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 510,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "2883a95a_b72a7859",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "libcutils/ashmem-dev.cpp",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 516,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 519,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "        struct stat sb;\n\n        if (fstat(fd, \u0026sb) \u003d\u003d -1) {\n            ALOGE(\"ashmem_get_name(%d): fstat failed: %m\", fd);\n            return nullptr;\n        }\n\n        strncpy(_name, sb.st_dev, ASHMEM_NAME_LEN);\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "07f3b22131a4f19ef88eaa3b25afcc0ee4292cad",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
