        "id": 1934715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-25T23:16:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should also be checking the return value of `readlink()` for errors. In the case there isn\u0027t an error, we should use the amount of bytes printed to add a null terminator, since `readlink()` doesn\u0027t do that by default [1].\n\n[1] https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/readlink.2.html",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 518,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 518,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "3452747b_10b1bfc1",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "libcutils/ashmem-dev.cpp",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 518,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 519,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "        int len \u003d readlink(path, _name, ASHMEM_NAME_LEN);\n        if (len \u003c 0) {\n            ALOGE(\"ashmem_get_name(%d) failed: %s\", fd, strerror(errno));\n            return nullptr;\n        }\n        _name[len] \u003d \u0027\\0\u0027;\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "07f3b22131a4f19ef88eaa3b25afcc0ee4292cad",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
