        "id": 1934715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-25T23:16:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note: the ashmem driver will either return the default name(/dev/ashmem)--if no name has been set--or the name that was used with `ASHMEM_SET_NAME`. So for example, if you just allocate an ashmem buffer, and don\u0027t name it, you will get `/dev/ashmem`. If you name it test-buf, you will get \"test-buf\".\n\nI think we should do the same thing for memfd and strip out the \"/memfd:\" prefix and the \" (deleted)\" suffix.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 520,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 524,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "dfeadab0_a2ec1cf5",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "libcutils/ashmem-dev.cpp",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 516,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 519,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "        struct stat sb;\n\n        if (fstat(fd, \u0026sb) \u003d\u003d -1) {\n            ALOGE(\"ashmem_get_name(%d): fstat failed: %m\", fd);\n            return nullptr;\n        }\n\n        _name \u003d (char*)malloc(sb.st_size + 1);\n        if (!_name) {\n            return nullptr;\n        }\n\n        ssize_t len \u003d readlink(android::base::StringPrintf(\"/proc/self/fd/%d\", fd).c_str(), _name, sb.st_size);\n        if (len \u003d\u003d -1) {\n            ALOGE(\"ashmem_get_name(%d): readlink failed: %m\", fd);\n            free(_name);\n            return nullptr;\n        }\n\n        _name[len] \u003d \u0027\\0\u0027;\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
